  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.0.13: Upgraded the bundled Zebra AI DataCapture SDK from 3.2.8 to 3.3.0\n      for faster, more reliable barcode decoding. No API changes. Models bundled\n      via satellite packages stay the same: barcode-localizer 5.0.2, text-ocr-recognizer 2.8.1.\n      v1.0.12: Stack rebuilt with Kotlin 2.3.20, AGP 9.1, CameraX 1.6.0, compileSdk 36,\n      serialization 1.11.0, coroutines 1.10.2. Fix: in barcode-only (or ocr-only)\n      mode only one detector is attached to the EntityTrackerAnalyzer, preventing\n      the 'Image queue is full' saturation introduced by CameraX 1.6.\n      MAUI consumers must explicitly declare\n      <PackageReference Include=\"Xamarin.AndroidX.Camera.Camera2.Pipe\" Version=\"1.6.0\"\n        ExcludeAssets=\"all\" GeneratePathProperty=\"true\" />\n      and re-inject the raw AAR via <AndroidLibrary Bind=\"false\"/> to avoid\n      the XA4217 binding generator failure on the Kotlin method with value class.\n      v1.0.11: CatturaScanner.Initialize() now auto-pre-loads AI decoders\n      in background when called with an Activity context (no extra API call\n      needed). Use Platform.CurrentActivity from MAUI OnAppearing.\n      v1.0.10: Added CatturaScanner.PreloadDecoders(activity) — pre-loads\n      AI decoders in background after Initialize() so the first Scan()\n      starts the camera immediately instead of showing the \"Initializing AI\n      engine\" overlay for several seconds. Must be called from an Activity\n      context so JNI gets the correct classloader.\n      v1.0.9: Detect non-AI-capable Zebra devices upfront via ro.soc.model\n      (e.g. TC22 with QCM5430): CatturaScanner.Scan() returns\n      CatturaError.CODE_SDK_NOT_AVAILABLE immediately instead of opening\n      the camera and silently failing. Added BarcodeOverlayLabelSizeSp\n      and OcrOverlayLabelSizeSp on CatturaConfig (10-40 sp, default 18).\n      Overlay boxes now use distinct colors: green for barcode, blue for OCR.\n      v1.0.8: Added CatturaScanner.ShowDeviceId(context) public API — shows AlertDialog with\n      model + device ID + Copy button, and logs values to logcat (tag: Cattura.SDK).\n      v1.0.7: Added CatturaScanner.GetDeviceId(context) public API for license activation;\n      device info section (model + device ID + copy button) added to settings panel;\n      LicenseValidator uses 5-level fallback chain for device identifier (Android 14 compatible).",
